                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3c911934-2c55-4b82-96c4-a3e3e3cd4811",
                        "entry_id": "17e38e0d-ae02-3d20-939d-18ed5bbe541c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "craintives"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e00d3ab2-712c-33ce-8df1-121b97b349de",
                        "entry_id": "17e38e0d-ae02-3d20-939d-18ed5bbe541c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est sujet à la crainte."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1db2536d-7540-4c1c-98fa-4f0191b21d49",
                                "sense_id": "e00d3ab2-712c-33ce-8df1-121b97b349de",
                                "text": "Après cet affreux, ce double malheur, Modeste devenue fille unique, sans que son père le sût, rendit Dumay, non pas plus dévoué, mais plus craintif que par le passé."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36fc9bd3-66b5-4639-ba05-df7b68824377",
                                "sense_id": "e00d3ab2-712c-33ce-8df1-121b97b349de",
                                "text": "Dès la Saint-Nicolas, on aperçut des loups. Pas les fauves habituels des hivers rigoureux, qui trottinaient vers nous des forêts morvandiaudes, le poil roussâtre, l’échine arquée, craintifs de l’homme."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "88c918c2-b207-4de9-9590-0e21d086dfbc",
                        "source_entry_id": "17e38e0d-ae02-3d20-939d-18ed5bbe541c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e00d3ab2-712c-33ce-8df1-121b97b349de",
                        "target_lang_word": "fearful",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fearful",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57739382-f0e1-34ee-b4a7-b834a68e82df",
                                        "entry_id": "d52fbcc3-92b7-3d5f-8fa1-03097f3da578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Frightening; causing fear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be41e871-4f55-4fce-96b5-b98646dc0820",
                                                "sense_id": "57739382-f0e1-34ee-b4a7-b834a68e82df",
                                                "text": "Sirs, stop their mouths, let them not speak to me,\nBut let them hear what fearful words I utter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6660a689-a025-481e-8779-2ebcdb92969c",
                                                "sense_id": "57739382-f0e1-34ee-b4a7-b834a68e82df",
                                                "text": "In the later Hebrew midrash Lilith is presented as the woman who knows how to recite the fearful name of God to work calamity; that this little girl cries out the fearful name of the sun god and thereby causes an earthquake would indicate that this girl is linked in the structure of the myth with Lilith."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f1ea97a-54d9-36b9-b42e-e7a9a692e867",
                                        "entry_id": "d52fbcc3-92b7-3d5f-8fa1-03097f3da578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tending to fear; timid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "acbba78c-fec1-42b2-bda4-c9c31686d6b7",
                                                "sense_id": "6f1ea97a-54d9-36b9-b42e-e7a9a692e867",
                                                "text": "a fearful boy"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1d956c5-1812-3215-b615-f25ff0466185",
                                        "entry_id": "d52fbcc3-92b7-3d5f-8fa1-03097f3da578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Terrible; shockingly bad."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01f759f5-53d6-471c-8add-a60fad61da5b",
                                                "sense_id": "f1d956c5-1812-3215-b615-f25ff0466185",
                                                "text": "But every day after dinner, for an hour, we were all together, and then the Favourite and the rest of the Royal Hareem competed who should most beguile the leisure of the Serene Haroun reposing from the cares of State — which were generally, as in most affairs of State, of an arithmetical character, the Commander of the Faithful being a fearful boggler at a sum."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "216c9d5d-019c-3c9f-9e7e-1d87f5cda136",
                                        "entry_id": "d52fbcc3-92b7-3d5f-8fa1-03097f3da578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Frightened; filled with terror."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ad73032-828f-422a-87ab-54dc6336778f",
                                                "sense_id": "216c9d5d-019c-3c9f-9e7e-1d87f5cda136",
                                                "text": "kings ſhall crouch vnto our conquering ſwords,\nAnd hoſtes of Souldiers ſtand amazd at vs,\nWhen with their fearfull tongues they ſhall confeſſe\nTheſe are the men that al the world admires,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d7f792f-848d-48d9-99c6-e1808a16465a",
                                                "sense_id": "216c9d5d-019c-3c9f-9e7e-1d87f5cda136",
                                                "text": "Those two great champions did attonce pursew / The fearefull damzell with incessant payns […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fearful",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a41a3b64-37b1-3b83-a8af-b4ec72d66b59",
                                        "entry_id": "7e2b64df-f4d9-3469-94a8-3031097bc4bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Extremely; fearfully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82e2baae-7359-4828-b2dc-5c4864dc1f9f",
                                                "sense_id": "a41a3b64-37b1-3b83-a8af-b4ec72d66b59",
                                                "text": "“He is fearful handsome, as you know,” she said remorsefully, “you cannot imagine, Georgiana, the joy when I first fell in love with him.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e96bdee-e266-4af5-a71f-925595f51741",
                                                "sense_id": "a41a3b64-37b1-3b83-a8af-b4ec72d66b59",
                                                "text": "“It's a fearful strong charm needs dragon's blood,” he said plaintively."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8113104b-84bd-47bc-9d98-ebd6bd1182cb",
                                                "sense_id": "a41a3b64-37b1-3b83-a8af-b4ec72d66b59",
                                                "text": "His Dardanelles expedition gave the Turk a fearful long start."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0e704688-4527-4391-b87d-78d0d408be54",
                        "source_entry_id": "17e38e0d-ae02-3d20-939d-18ed5bbe541c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e00d3ab2-712c-33ce-8df1-121b97b349de",
                        "target_lang_word": "apprehensive",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "apprehensive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e602083d-74ad-3e39-9949-b1f4aa34868f",
                                        "entry_id": "cf2e1823-0c5f-3854-80a0-39619ceec87e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anticipating something with anxiety, fear, or doubt; reluctant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "681c7311-1812-429d-8638-17f5ea8991a2",
                                                "sense_id": "e602083d-74ad-3e39-9949-b1f4aa34868f",
                                                "text": "This convinc'd me that there was no going on Shore for us in the Night upon that Coaſt, and how to venture on Shore in the Day was another Queſtion too; for to have fallen into the Hands of any of the Savages, had been as bad as to have fallen into the Hands of Lyons and Tygers; at leaſt we were equally apprehenſive of the Danger of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83a71d25-d17b-4e7d-900e-6ccf797bbeb2",
                                                "sense_id": "e602083d-74ad-3e39-9949-b1f4aa34868f",
                                                "text": "But Claggart's was no vulgar form of the passion. Nor, as directed toward Billy Budd, did it partake of that streak of apprehensive jealousy that marred Saul's visage perturbedly brooding on the comely young David. Claggart's envy struck deeper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16e468ab-7a38-4431-b8f3-dc54d043ea58",
                                                "sense_id": "e602083d-74ad-3e39-9949-b1f4aa34868f",
                                                "text": "Never before in his life had Dan Holland feared anything, but now he was apprehensive for the safety of this trim blond creature before him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73c4a875-3797-3f2e-b7da-631f76a3600f",
                                        "entry_id": "cf2e1823-0c5f-3854-80a0-39619ceec87e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Perceptive; quick to learn; capable of understanding using one's intellect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ace1d387-68c2-4b72-ba26-33287bb5cf34",
                                                "sense_id": "73c4a875-3797-3f2e-b7da-631f76a3600f",
                                                "text": "More fond of Miracles, than apprehensive of Truth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "apprehensive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f9a957b-7ec3-36c4-93fe-de30bc4d233c",
                                        "entry_id": "e847b2f4-6f6e-3fec-a26e-4e504629761b",
                                        "glosses": [
